{
  "$comment": "What a noun IS to a making. An element's tags say what it belongs to; they do not say what part it plays when something is made from it. Marble and Mausolus are both inputs to the Mausoleum: one is the stuff, the other is the man it was built for, and no tag distinguishes them. This file writes that fact down so tools/places.mjs can check derivation exactly instead of guessing from tags. Scope: every input to a place recipe. Extend it as other checks need it; a partial file is honest as long as the tools that read it only ask about ids it covers.",
  "$roles": {
    "material": "The stuff the thing is made of. Contributes to the making.",
    "technique": "A learned human way of making or shaping: a plan, a joint, a style, a survey. Contributes.",
    "process": "A natural process that shapes without intent: erosion, a flood, a volcano. Contributes.",
    "tool": "An instrument, machine or vehicle used in the making. Contributes.",
    "maker": "The agency that caused it: a person, a people, a state, a trade, an institution, an economic system, an era standing for its people. Contributes.",
    "site": "The ground, water or region the thing occupies. Says where, not how. Does not contribute.",
    "form": "The kind of thing it is: a castle, a temple, a statue. Says what, not how. Does not contribute.",
    "occupant": "A living thing or object present at it but not part of its making. Does not contribute.",
    "subject": "What it depicts, honours, serves or commemorates. Mausolus is the subject of the Mausoleum; Artemisia II is its maker. Does not contribute.",
    "evidence": "How the thing is known or dated, not how it was made. Does not contribute."
  },
  "$contributes": [
    "material",
    "technique",
    "process",
    "tool",
    "maker"
  ],
